{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And the name of the slain man of Israel.</b> Just as Scripture traces the lineage of the righteous to their praise, so it traces the lineage of the wicked to their disgrace, to teach you that whoever blemishes himself blemishes his family." "<b>A prince of a father's house among the Simeonites.</b> He was a prince of a father's house — one of the five father's houses that the tribe of Simeon had. And concerning him it is said (Ecclesiastes 10:8): ״ופורץ גדר ישכנו נחש״ — and he who breaches a fence, a serpent shall bite him. Simeon his father had fenced against harlotry in the episode of Shechem with Dinah, when he said (Genesis 34:31): ״הכזונה יעשה את אחותנו״, and now the son came and breached that fence."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:36:06.020826221Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}